.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-quick-archive 1  "tapectl-quick-archive " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-quick\-archive \- Quick archive: create + stage + write in one flow
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl quick\-archive\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-\-tenant\fR> [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] <\fB\-\-volume\fR> [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-tag\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-device\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPATH\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Quick archive: create + stage + write in one flow
.PP
The volume must already exist — run `tapectl volume init LABEL \-\-device /dev/nstN` first. This command creates the unit, snapshot and stage set, but not the volume.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR \fI<TENANT>\fR
Tenant name
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes. Commands that cannot preview refuse the flag rather than ignore it (issue #241)
.TP
\fB\-\-volume\fR \fI<VOLUME>\fR
Label of an ALREADY\-INITIALIZED volume to write to. Create it with `tapectl volume init LABEL \-\-device ...`; quick\-archive does not
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-tag\fR \fI<TAG>\fR
Tags
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-\-device\fR \fI<DEVICE>\fR
Tape device (by\-id path). Defaults to the only configured drive; required when more than one is configured
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip ADR\-0008 Tier\-2 confirmation prompts. It never reaches a Tier\-3 refusal — those are facts, not risks to accept (issue #147)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file.

NOTE: on its own this ALSO relocates the whole tapectl home to the config file\*(Aqs parent directory — database, keys, staging, receipts. That is how every test harness gets an isolated home, so it still works, but it is surprising enough that it now warns. Use \-\-home when you mean "operate on a different archive", and \-\-config only to point at a config file inside that home (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
tapectl home directory: database, keys, catalogs, receipts, logs.

Defaults to ~/.tapectl. The config file is taken from <home>/config.toml unless \-\-config overrides it. Also settable as TAPECTL_HOME (issue #109).
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path to directory
